# 🧅 Hardened Tor Client Configuration (Maximum Opsec & Anti-DNS Leak)

This repository stores the ultimate, audited **`torrc`** blueprint optimized for local client anonymity, aggressive circuit rotation, and strict DNS leak protection [~ ➜]. This profile is specifically built to operate securely behind consumer-grade internet connections [~ ➜].

---

## 🔒 The Hardened Configuration Blueprint

```ini
# Configuração Base de Cliente
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050

# Desativa completamente o Relay (Segurança contra CGNAT)
ORPort 0
DirPort 0

# Rotação agressiva de circuitos (Muda de IP de saída a cada 2 minutos)
MaxCircuitDirtiness 120

# Proteção Avançada de Anonimato
CircuitPadding 1
ReducedConnectionPadding 0
SafeLogging 1
Log notice file /var/log/tor/notices.log

# Prevenção Absoluta de Vazamento de DNS (DNS Leak)
DNSPort 127.0.0.1:53530
AutomapHostsOnResolve 1
AutomapHostsSuffixes .onion,.exit
TestSocks 1
```

---

## 🔬 Architectural Security Breakdown

### 🛡️ 1. CGNAT Isolation & Zero-Inbound Footprint (`ORPort 0`)
*   By explicitly pinning `ORPort 0` and `DirPort 0`, the Tor daemon acts strictly as an **outbound client node** [~ ➜]. 
*   It closes all external listening ports, making your host completely invisible to external network scans and fully compatible with **CGNAT (Carrier-Grade NAT)** setups where port forwarding is restricted [~ ➜].

### ⚡ 2. Aggressive Circuit Rotation (`MaxCircuitDirtiness 120`)
*   Standard Tor installations keep an exit node identity alive for 10 minutes. This configuration drops that threshold down to **120 seconds (2 minutes)** [~ ➜].
*   Your automation scripts and browser sessions will aggressively rotate their public exit node IPs, severely disrupting behavioral tracking, timing attacks, and endpoint correlation [~ ➜].

### 🕵️‍♂️ 3. Anti-DNS Leak Matrix (`DNSPort` & `AutomapHosts`)
*   **`DNSPort 127.0.0.1:53530`**: Opens a local secure DNS proxy [~ ➜]. Any system script mapping domain names through this port automatically pushes the plaintext payload straight into the encrypted Onion wrapper, bypassing local ISP resolvers entirely [~ ➜].
*   **`AutomapHostsOnResolve 1`**: Intercepts map lookups for `.onion` and virtual `.exit` zones, preventing your local system from leaking hidden service descriptors to vanilla upstream name servers [~ ➜].

